TX_THREAD_SECURE_STACK_MAXIMUM|TX_THREAD_SECURE_STACK_MAXIMUM|Core||=TX_THREAD_SECURE_STACK_MINIMUM|10240|Define the maximum stack for a ThreadX secure thread on this processor
STACK_MINIMUM|STACK_MINIMUM|||||
STACK_MAXIMUM|STACK_MAXIMUM|||||
TX_ENABLE_BASEPRI_SUPPORT|Enable BASEPRI support|Core||||When enabled ThreadX will use the Base Priority Mask Register
TX_BASEPRI_VALUE|TX_BASEPRI_VALUE|Core||0|15|When the value is set to a nonzero ThreeadX will prevent the activation of exception with a same priority or lower than the TX_BASEPRI_VALUE Min : 0 no Effect (default value) Max: (2 ^ __NVIC_PRIO_BITS) -1
TX_PORT_BASEPRI_VALUE|TX_PORT_BASEPRI_VALUE|Core||0|12332315|
TX_DISABLE_ERROR_CHECKING|TX_DISABLE_ERROR_CHECKING|Core||||Defined, the basic parameter error checking is disabled.
THREADX_MEM_POOL_VAR_NAME|ThreadX MemPool Name|Memory Configuration||||Default ThreadX memory pool var name. <font color="red"> <b>This is a variable name. It should be C compliant declaration, Otherwise compilation errors will be generated in the project. </b> </font>
FILEX_MEM_POOL_VAR_NAME|FileX MemPool Name|Memory Configuration||||Default memory pool size for the FileX application.
USBX_HOST_MEM_POOL_VAR_NAME|USBXHost MemPool Name|Memory Configuration||||Default memory pool size for the USBXHost application.
USBX_DEVICE_MEM_POOL_VAR_NAME|USBXDevice MemPool Name|Memory Configuration||||Default memory pool size for the USBXDevice application.
NETXDUO_MEM_POOL_VAR_NAME|NetXDuo MemPool Name|Memory Configuration||||Default memory pool size for the USBXDevice application.
TX_APP_GENERATE_INIT_CODE|Generate App Init Code|ThreadX App Init||||Giving the access to generate the following application code: <li>Create ThreadX Application Thread.</li> <li>Create ThreadX Application Semaphore.</li> <li>Create ThreadX Application Mutex.</li> <li>Create ThreadX Application MessageQueue.</li>
TX_APP_CREATION|Create ThreadX Application Thread|ThreadX App Init||N/A|N/A|Enable the allocation and creation of the thread.
TX_APP_THREAD_ENTRY|ThreadX Application Thread Entry|ThreadX App Init||||Main thread entry function Name.
TX_APP_THREAD_NAME|ThreadX Application Thread Name|ThreadX App Init||||ThreadX Application thread Name.
TX_APP_THREAD_PRIO|ThreadX Application Thread Priority|ThreadX App Init||0|=TX_MAX_PRIORITIES|Default ThreadX Application Thread Priority value for ThreadX application. ThreadX Application Thread Priority must be between 0 and TX_MAX_PRIORITIES.
TX_APP_STACK_SIZE|ThreadX Application Thread Stack Size|ThreadX App Init||512|=TX_APP_MEM_POOL_SIZE|Default thread stack size value for ThreadX application.
TX_APP_SEM_CREATION|Create ThreadX Application Semaphore|ThreadX App Init||||Generate application code to initialize the ThreadX App Semaphore.
TX_SEMAPHORE_NAME|ThreadX Application Semaphore Name|ThreadX App Init||||ThreadX Application Semaphore Name.
TX_SEMAPHORE_COUNT|ThreadX Application Semaphore Init Count|ThreadX App Init||0|1024|Initial value for counting semaphores.
TX_APP_MUTEX_CREATION|Create ThreadX Application Mutex|ThreadX App Init||||Generate application code to initialize the ThreadX App Mutex.
TX_MUTEX_NAME|ThreadX Application Mutex Name|ThreadX App Init||||ThreadX Application Mutex Name.
TX_MUTEX_INHERITANCE|ThreadX Application Mutex Inheritance Support|ThreadX App Init||||Enable priority inheritance feature: TX_NO_INHERIT / TX_INHERIT Specifies whether or not this mutex supports priority inheritance. If this value is TX_INHERIT, then priority inheritance is supported. However, if TX_NO_INHERIT is specified, priority inheritance is not supported by this mutex.
TX_APP_MSG_QUEUE_CREATION|Create ThreadX Application MessageQueue|ThreadX App Init||||Generate application code to initialize the ThreadX App MessageQueue.
TX_MSG_QUEUE_NAME|ThreadX Application Queue Name|ThreadX App Init||||ThreadX Application MessageQueue Name.
TX_MSG_SIZE_WORDS|ThreadX Application Queue Message Size in words|ThreadX App Init||1|16|The size of a single message in words.
TX_NB_MSG|ThreadX Application Number of Messages|ThreadX App Init||1|512|The total number of messages in a Queue.

